  "body": "What failed: the batch gate on main 872901a2 ended red on one test, `mcp_pick_in_box_adds_the_rim_in_one_undo_step` (crates/app/tests/box_pick.rs). Panic at line 220: `import_model refused: \"import_model: I/O error: The system cannot find the path specified. (os error 3)\"`. The other 6 tests of the binary passed.\nWhere: gate log `gate-logs/batch-20261113-021709/07-app_suites_slow_release_tier_center_cut_multiaxis_.log` (local, main checkout).\n\nCause (read from origin/main, not re-run): `write_plate_stl()` builds `temp_dir()/camcraft-box-pick-<process id>/plate.stl`, and it starts with `remove_dir_all(dir)` then `create_dir_all`. Two tests in the same binary call it (`mcp_pick_in_box_adds_the_rim_in_one_undo_step`, line 216, and `mcp_pick_in_box_is_visible_only_unless_through`, line 266). The dir name depends only on the pid, so both tests use the same directory. Under parallel test threads, one test's `remove_dir_all` deletes the dir (and the STL) the other has just written, and its `import_model` gets os error 3 (path not found).\n\nIntroduced by: the second test arrived with commit 8e820f01 \"fix(pick): the box honours Pick through; MCP pick_in_box takes through\" (PR #1078, issue #979); the helper itself is from 6716fad1 (same PR).\n\nDeterministic? No, a race. It fails only when the two tests overlap in the window between write and import, so it is intermittent (hit once in this gate run, 6 of 7 passed).\n\nFix direction: give each call a unique dir (an atomic counter or the test name in the dir name, as other suites do), and do not rely on remove-then-create of a shared path.\n\nDone means: `write_plate_stl` returns a path unique per call; `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test box_pick` passes repeatedly (e.g. 10 runs) with default threads.\n",
